        .init(id: "fermentation", title: "Recycle and repeat", stage: "Without oxygen · Fermentation", mnemonic: "Regenerate NAD⁺. Keep glycolysis going.", duration: 8, playerID: "fermentation", accessibility: "Fermentation uses neither oxygen nor an electron transport chain. It regenerates NAD plus from NADH, allowing glycolysis to continue making two net ATP per glucose. Alcoholic fermentation produces ethanol and carbon dioxide, as in yeast for bread and beer. Lactic acid fermentation produces lactate, as in Lactobacillus in yogurt and human muscle during oxygen debt. Delayed soreness is linked to microscopic muscle damage, not lactate buildup.", bullets: ["**No O₂. No electron transport chain.** All **2 net ATP per glucose** come from **glycolysis**.","Transferring electrons from **NADH** into fermentation products regenerates **NAD⁺**, allowing glycolysis to continue.","**Alcoholic:** pyruvate → **ethanol + CO₂**. Example: **yeast** in **bread and beer**.","**Lactic acid:** pyruvate → **lactate (lactic acid)**. Examples: **Lactobacillus** in **yogurt** and **human muscle during oxygen debt**.","**Delayed muscle soreness:** linked to **microscopic muscle damage**, not lactate buildup."]),
